uint32_t block_action_rm(ivec3 pos, unsigned type, plid from) ->
<var>type</var>=0 invokes undefined behvaior.
Destroys a set of blocks in bulk. Call this multiple times, followed by block_action_cull() given the return value of each call to this as <var>mask</var>, followed by finish_cull().

<p>The solidity of any given voxel on the map is unspecified between a call to this and finish_cull().
Calling any function that modifies the map between a call to this and the next instance of either block_action_cull() or finish_cull() invokes undefined behavior.
If block_action_cull() is not called with the return value of this function before the next call to finish_cull(), invokes undefined behavior.

<p>Calls send_block_action() if the map isn't currently loading.
See send_block_action() for values of <var>type</var>.

void block_action_cull(ivec3 pos, uint32_t mask) ->
Call this between a series of calls to block_action_rm() and finish_cull() with the return value of block_action_rm() as <var>mask</var>, and with the same <var>pos</var>.
Otherwise, your local dinosaur sets off a nuclear chain reaction.

void finish_cull(void) ->
Cleans up after block_action_rm() and block_action_cull().

void block_action(ivec3 pos, unsigned type, plid from) ->
Places or destroys a set of blocks.
Calls send_block_action() if <var>type</var>=<kbd>0</kbd> and the map isn't currently loading. <!-- TODO: a lot more than this'll need to be unsent during mapload -->
<!-- TODO: need to get AoT zlibbing to work with this too. . . -->
If <var>type</var>&ne;<kbd>0</kbd>, calls block_action_rm(), block_action_cull() and finish_cull().
See send_block_action() for values of <var>type</var>.

